hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16746","He said: Abd Allah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn Humayd al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Dhu al-Ghurra, he said: A Bedouin intercepted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, and said: O Messenger of Allah, prayer overtakes us while we are in camel resting places, shall we pray in them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; he said: Shall we perform wudu from their meat; he said: Yes; he said: Shall we pray in sheep folds; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; he said: Shall we perform wudu from their meat; he said: No."
